    before: []  # fc25
    duplicate_of: []  # fc25
    not_duplicate_of: []  # fc25
    pr_ref:  # fc25
    description: "## Problem\n\nhtrac setup's _check_agents_md (check #16) scans AGENTS.md for tracker concepts but only warns\nabout missing content. It doesn't offer to inject or maintain tracker usage instructions. This\nmeans every repo adopting the tracker must manually write (or copy-paste) the usage rules, and\ntracker upgrades can't safely update those rules without clobbering project-specific policy.\n\n## Design: managed block with delimiter fencing\n\nSetup should manage content between delimiters:\n\n    <!-- BEGIN tracker-governance (managed by htrac setup — edits may be overwritten) -->\n    ...usage rules...\n    <!-- END tracker-governance -->\n\nThis block covers how to use the tracker correctly as a tool — rules that are true in any repo:\n\n1. Agent Context Protection — use show CLI, never read .ops files\n2. Auto-Sync — never manually commit .ops, don't include them in feature branches\n3. Task Selection — use ready not list for picking work\n4. Batching — batch updates into fewer commits\n5. Resolution Rationale — always --note when resolving items\n6. Unread Messages — check-messages workflow\n7. Quick reference — command cheat sheet\n8. Commit convention — tracker: prefix\n\nThe block ends with a handoff sentence: \"Configure which statuses block agent stopping, and\nwhat each status means for agent behavior, in your project's governance policy.\"\n\n## What the managed block must NOT contain\n\nAnything about what statuses mean for agent workflow:\n- Which statuses block stopping\n- What investigation depth each status implies (e.g., \"assume structural\")\n- The decision tree for choosing statuses\n- Circuit breaker thresholds and stop-hook integration\n- The Scope Expansion Commitment Protocol\n\nThese are project-governance decisions. The tracker ships status labels (violated, todo_hard,\netc.) via config.yaml, but their behavioral semantics belong to the project.\n\n## Wizard behavior\n\n- If AGENTS.md exists with no delimiters: insert the block at the end of the nearest\n  ### Tracker section, or create one. Warn the user.\n- If AGENTS.md exists with delimiters: replace content between them. Preserve everything\n  outside.\n- If no AGENTS.md: create a minimal one with just the tracker block, plus a comment suggesting\n  the user add project-level policy.\n- Optional --with-policy-template flag: emit a separate, non-managed ### Tracker Status Policy\n  section after the END delimiter, with a status table, decision tree, and stop-hook integration\n  as scaffolding the user owns. The wizard never touches this section again.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis item covers changes to hypergumbo-tracker's setup.py only. It does NOT modify hypergumbo's\nown AGENTS.md. The managed block content is defined in the tracker package as a constant or\ntemplate, and setup injects it into whatever AGENTS.md exists in the target repo.\n\n## Why this is needs_human_review\n\nChanges to how governance content is injected into AGENTS.md are themselves governance-adjacent.\nThe managed block content, the delimiter convention, and the --with-policy-template scaffolding\nall need human sign-off before implementation."  # fc25
    fields: {}  # fc25
